{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrix","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.SkeinPolynomialTransferMatrix","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DoubleBetaCrossTerm.cross_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DoubleBetaCrossTerm.cross_term","kind":"def","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L218-L218","doc":"The cross-term Δ_{p₁p₂}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DoubleBetaCrossTerm.P_beta2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DoubleBetaCrossTerm.P_beta2","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L216-L216","doc":"Single-beta₂ daughter value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DoubleBetaCrossTerm.P_beta1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DoubleBetaCrossTerm.P_beta1","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L214-L214","doc":"Single-beta₁ daughter value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DoubleBetaCrossTerm.P_2beta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DoubleBetaCrossTerm.P_2beta","kind":"def","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L212-L212","doc":"Double-beta daughter value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DoubleBetaCrossTerm.P_par","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DoubleBetaCrossTerm.P_par","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L210-L210","doc":"Parent Skein polynomial value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DoubleBetaCrossTerm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DoubleBetaCrossTerm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L208-L208","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DoubleBetaCrossTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DoubleBetaCrossTerm","kind":"structure","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L200-L219","doc":"Double beta decay: the 2-jet cross-term is nonzero.\nP^(2β) - P^(par) ≠ (P^(β₁) - P^(par)) + (P^(β₂) - P^(par))\nThe difference is the nuclear matrix element polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.Q_q_from_polynomials","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.Q_q_from_polynomials","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L190-L198","doc":"The Q_q-value as the difference of Skein polynomials at q.\n\nQ_q = P_par(q) - P_dau(q) - P_e(q)\n\nThis is a polynomial in q evaluated at the physical point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.triple_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.triple_identity","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L176-L184","doc":"All three roles of the canonical bundle use the same numerical\nvalue: the Descartes substrate parameter equals `q` and the Hecke\ndeformation coefficient equals `q − 1/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity.ofQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity.ofQ","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L169-L174","doc":"The canonical triple-identity bundle built from a single `q > 1`,\ntaking every role from its structural default. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity.descartes_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity.descartes_q","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L167-L167","doc":"Physical role: the Descartes substrate parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity.skein_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity.skein_eval","kind":"def","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L165-L165","doc":"Topological role: evaluated Skein polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity.hecke_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity.hecke_coeff","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L163-L163","doc":"Algebraic role: the Hecke deformation coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L161-L161","doc":"q > 1 (non-classical). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity.q","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L159-L159","doc":"The single parameter q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L157-L157","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstrateTripleIdentity","kind":"structure","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L149-L167","doc":"The three roles of q are the same parameter.\n\n1. Algebraic: σ² = (q - q⁻¹)σ + 1 (Hecke deformation)\n2. Topological: variable of P_N(q) (Skein polynomial)\n3. Physical: q = 1.1097 (Descartes condition χ = -6)\n\nThis structure bundles all three roles. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.transfer_matrix_steps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.transfer_matrix_steps","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L117-L143","doc":"The total number of transfer matrix multiplications is C(A,2).\nThis is exact — not an asymptotic bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skein_polynomial_degree_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skein_polynomial_degree_bound","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L97-L111","doc":"The degree of P_N(q) as a polynomial in q^½ is ≤ A² - 1.\n\nEach generator σ_i has k_i = A-i-1 crossings, contributing\ndegree ≤ 2k_i + 1 to the polynomial. Summing:\nΣ(2k_i + 1) = 2·C(A,2) + (A-1) = A(A-1) + (A-1) = A² - 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skeinPolynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skeinPolynomial","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L87-L91","doc":"The nuclear Skein polynomial: product of traced volumes.\nP_N(q) = Π_i V̂_i(q). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tracedVolumeFromMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tracedVolumeFromMatrix","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L61-L85","doc":"The traced volume at generator σ_i: V̂_i(q) = z · a_i + b_i,\nwhere (a_i, b_i) come from the transfer matrix product M_i and `z` is the\nMarkov parameter in **convention D**, `z = q³/(q² + 1)`.\n\n**Migrated from convention C 2026-08-26 (bean `qou-cxjq` step 3).** This read\n`z = 1/(√q + 1/√q) = √q/(q+1)`, which is convention C — excised by owner\nruling R1 of 2026-08-15. The migration is a **change of shape, not a change\nof variable**: `QOU.BraidKnot.no_kernel_instantiation_is_conventionD` proves\nthat for every `q > 1` no real `u` at all satisfies `u/(u²+1) = q³/(q²+1)`,\nso no substitution `s² = q` could have done this. See\n`QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovConventionSeparation.lean`.\n\nSafe to migrate in place here: `tracedVolumeFromMatrix` has **no references\nanywhere in the tree** outside this definition, and none of this file's three\ntheorems mentions it — so no recorded statement silently changes meaning.\n(That is the failure mode the five-way `markovZ` overload created, and it is\nwhy the convention is now named in the docstring rather than left to be\ninferred from the formula.)\n\nNo longer a polynomial in `q^½`: convention D is rational in `q` itself,\nwhich is the point of the convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.crossingMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.crossingMatrix","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L49-L55","doc":"Transfer matrix for a single crossing with coefficients (c, d). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix.id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix.id","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L44-L47","doc":"The identity transfer matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix.mul","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L36-L42","doc":"Transfer matrix multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix.a₂₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix.a₂₂","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix.a₂₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix.a₂₁","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix.a₁₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix.a₁₂","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix.a₁₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix.a₁₁","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix.mk","kind":"ctor","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix","kind":"structure","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-polynomial-transfer-matrix.lean#L28-L34","doc":"A 2×2 transfer matrix with entries in ℝ (specialized from ℤ[q^±½]). ","signatureChunk":0}]}